{
  "tema": 5085,
  "slug": "me-levanto-reflexivos-presente",
  "titulo": "Reflexive verbs in the present",
  "subtitulo": "Me levanto, me baño y me voy.",
  "foto": "t07.jpg",
  "regla": "Reflexive verbs (infinitive in -se) use a pronoun that matches the subject, placed before the conjugated verb: me levanto, te levantas, se levanta, nos levantamos, se levantan.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": null,
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "A reflexive verb ends in **-se** in the dictionary: **levantarse** (_to get up_), **ducharse** (_to shower_), **llamarse** (_to be called_)."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Conjugate the verb as usual and put the matching pronoun **before** it."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Person",
            "levantarse"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "yo",
              "**me** levanto"
            ],
            [
              "tú",
              "**te** levantas"
            ],
            [
              "él / ella / usted",
              "**se** levanta"
            ],
            [
              "nosotros / nosotras",
              "**nos** levantamos"
            ],
            [
              "ellos / ellas / ustedes",
              "**se** levantan"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "The pronoun always matches the subject: **yo → me**, **nosotros → nos**. In the present it never goes after the verb."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "==Me levanto== a las cinco para surfear.",
              "en": "I get up at five to go surfing."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿A qué hora ==te bañas==?",
              "en": "What time do you take a shower?"
            },
            {
              "es": "Mi papá ==se rasura== todos los días.",
              "en": "My dad shaves every day."
            },
            {
              "es": "Después del jiu-jitsu ==nos duchamos== en el gimnasio.",
              "en": "After jiu-jitsu we shower at the gym."
            },
            {
              "es": "Los niños ==se lavan== los dientes.",
              "en": "The kids brush their teeth."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿Cómo ==se llama== tu maestra?",
              "en": "What's your teacher's name?"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "trampa",
      "titulo": "The trap",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "pares",
          "lista": [
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "Nosotros se levantamos tarde."
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "Nosotros nos levantamos tarde."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "nosotros → **nos**."
            },
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "Levanto me a las siete."
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "Me levanto a las siete."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "Before the conjugated verb."
            },
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "Tú se duchas en la noche."
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "Tú te duchas en la noche."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "tú → **te**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "parientes",
      "titulo": "Related rules",
      "bloques": [
